<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Mason (governor)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1586–<a href="/years/1635">1635</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Captain John Mason of New Hampshire</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-mason-connecticut">John Mason</a> was an English sea captain and colonial promoter who governed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> colony at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cupids">Cuper's Cove</a> from 1615 to about 1621. In 1622 he and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinando-gorges">Sir Ferdinando Gorges</a> received the land between the Merrimack and Kennebec rivers, and after they divided it in 1629 Mason took the western part, naming it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hampshire">New Hampshire</a> after his home county. He died in 1635 without visiting it.</p></div>
